@Tutorial(time: 10) {
    @Intro(title: "Exercise the deployed API") {
        Call the same OpenAPI routes you called locally, this time against the ALB DNS name, and watch the ECS task logs from CloudWatch.
    }

    @Section(title: "Post a TODO and read it back") {
        @ContentAndMedia {
            Point `curl` at the ALB DNS name. The Aurora cluster is a fresh database, so the first `POST` creates the first TODO. Then read it back with a `GET`.

            @Image(source: "aws-cloudwatch.svg", alt: "Amazon CloudWatch")
        }

        @Steps {
            @Step {
                **Capture** the ALB DNS name, then post a TODO.

                Read the DNS name from the `ServiceStack` CloudFormation output using `aws cloudformation describe-stacks`. Post a TODO and expect `201 Created`. On a cold start, the first request can take a few seconds while Aurora Serverless v2 scales up.

                @Code(name: "curl POST", file: 6-bash.8.txt, reset: true)
            }

            @Step {
                **Fetch** the TODOs and tail the task logs.

                A `GET` returns the item you just created. CDK generates the ECS log group name with a hash suffix, so look it up first with `aws logs describe-log-groups`, then `aws logs tail --follow` streams the ECS task logs from CloudWatch Logs.

                > Note: You will see repeated `warning swift-otel: ... Failed to export batch` / `Connection refused` lines alongside your request logs. This is expected. The app still exports OpenTelemetry (as it did against Grafana locally), but the deployed task has no OTel collector to receive it, so the exporter cannot reach `localhost:4318` and logs a warning. The app itself is healthy. Wiring an AWS OpenTelemetry backend is left as an advanced exercise: set the `OTEL_EXPORTER_OTLP_ENDPOINT` environment variable on the container in `aws-infra/lib/service-stack.ts` to point at a collector (for example a sidecar or the CloudWatch OTLP endpoint) that forwards to CloudWatch, X-Ray, or Amazon Managed Service for Prometheus.

                @Code(name: "curl GET and logs tail", file: 6-bash.9.txt, reset: true)
            }
        }
    }
}
